.\" Manual page for feagle. Keep it in sync with `feagle --help`: the test
.\" `tests/test_cli_docs.py` fails when a subcommand or an option is missing here.
.TH FEAGLE 1 "2026-10-19" "feagle 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
feagle \- local semantic file search for Arch Linux and Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B feagle
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
\fICOMMAND\fR
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B feagle
indexes the files under the configured roots and searches them in two ways: by
keywords (SQLite FTS5, BM25 ranking) and by meaning (vector embeddings from
.B llama-server
combined with the keyword hits through reciprocal rank fusion). Results carry a
position \- a line for text, a page for PDF, a timecode for media \- so that
.BR "feagle open" ,
or a launcher, can jump straight to the match.
.PP
Everything stays on the machine: there are no accounts, no telemetry and no
network traffic, except the model download that the user starts explicitly.
When
.B llama-server
or the model is missing, search degrades to the keyword index and
.B feagle doctor
says what to install for the semantic side.
.PP
A directory is watched by
.B feagle\-indexerd
and searched through the daemon
.BR feagle\-queryd ;
both are systemd user units. The command line talks to the search daemon when
it is running, and opens the database directly otherwise.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS index [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Scan the configured roots and bring the index up to date. Unchanged files are
not re-read: size and modification time are compared first, then a hash.
A pass over the configured roots also reconciles the index with the
configuration: a file that is gone, or that lies outside every configured root
(its directory was dropped from
.BR [index].roots ),
is removed. A pass with
.B \-\-root
only touches what it scans, and a pass paused by the load or battery check
removes nothing.
.TP
.BR \-\-root " " PATH
Index this directory instead of the configured roots. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-full
Re-extract and re-embed every file, even if it looks unchanged.
.TP
.B \-\-rebuild
Wipe the index (including stored vectors) and rebuild it from scratch.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-embed
Index text only; no embeddings are requested.
.TP
.B \-\-backfill
Embed the chunks of files that still lack vectors, for example after enabling
semantic search on an existing index.
.SS search [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIQUERY\fR
Search the index for
.IR QUERY .
.TP
.BR \-\-limit " " N
Return at most
.I N
results (default: from the configuration).
.TP
.BR \-\-mode " " MODE
One of
.BR auto ,
.B hybrid
or
.BR fts .
The default comes from the configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the raw JSON reply instead of the human\-readable list.
.TP
.B \-\-pick
Choose one of the results in a dmenu\-compatible launcher and open it.
.TP
.B \-\-with\-apps
Above the file results, also list matching desktop applications. Requires
.BR \-\-pick .
.SS status
Print what is in the index: files, chunks, vectors, coverage and the embedding
model.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the report as JSON.
.SS doctor [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Check the environment and dependencies (llama.cpp, the model file, poppler,
tesseract, the daemons, permissions) and print what to fix. It never changes
anything.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the report as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-fast
Skip hashing the model file (it is a few hundred MiB).
.SS setup [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Interactive first\-run setup: choose the roots, the launcher and the
performance profile, download and verify the model, write the configuration and
install the systemd user units.
.TP
.BR \-\-root " " PATH
Corpus directory to index. Repeatable; skips the interactive question.
.TP
.BR \-\-model " " PRESET|PATH
Model preset name, or a path to a GGUF file.
.TP
.BR \-\-mrl\-dim " " N
Truncate embeddings to
.I N
dimensions (Matryoshka models). One of 128, 256, 512, 768, 1024.
.TP
.BR \-\-launcher " " PROGRAM
Launcher for
.BR "feagle pick" :
.BR auto ,
.BR fuzzel ,
.BR wofi ,
.BR rofi ,
.BR tofi ,
.B walker
or
.BR stdout .
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Accept the defaults and do not ask anything.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-download
Do not download the model.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-units
Do not install the systemd user units.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-enable
Install the units but do not enable or start them.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-index
Skip the first indexing run.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-backup
Do not back up an existing configuration file before rewriting it.
.TP
.B \-\-media\-images
Enable image search (downloads the multimodal projector, about 530 MiB).
.TP
.B \-\-media\-video
Enable video frame indexing.
.TP
.B \-\-media\-audio
Enable audio transcription with whisper.cpp (downloads a model, about 148 MiB).
.SS open [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPATH\fR [\fIPOSITION\fR]
Open a file with the opener configured for its extension, at the given position.
.I POSITION
is
.I +N
for a line in text, or a page in a PDF.
.TP
.BR \-\-line " " N
Line number.
.TP
.BR \-\-page " " N
Page number (PDF).
.TP
.BR \-\-time " " SECONDS
Start time in seconds (audio, video).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the command that would be run instead of running it.
.SS pick [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Open a dmenu\-compatible launcher listing desktop applications and indexed
files. Applications come first. Without a configured launcher the list is
printed to stdout as
.IR key ", tab, description" .
.TP
.BR \-\-query " " TEXT
Rank the files semantically for this query instead of listing them by recency.
.TP
.BR \-\-limit " " N
How many results to show when
.B \-\-query
is given.
.TP
.BR \-\-files " " N
How many indexed files to list when there is no query (default: 500).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-apps
List files only.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-files
List applications only.
.SS queryd
Run the query daemon in the foreground; normally started by its systemd user
unit. It listens on a Unix socket and speaks line\-delimited JSON.
.SS indexerd [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Run the indexing daemon in the foreground; normally started by its systemd user
unit. It does an initial pass, then follows inotify events and rescans
periodically.
.TP
.BR \-\-root " " PATH
Watch this directory instead of the configured roots. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-once
Do a single indexing pass and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-poll
Poll the filesystem instead of using inotify (for network mounts and other
filesystems that do not deliver events).
.SS bench [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Run synthetic indexing and query benchmarks in an isolated runtime directory and
report throughput, latency, memory and database size.
.TP
.BR \-\-files " " N
Number of documents to generate (default: 60).
.TP
.BR \-\-seed " " N
Random seed for the generated corpus.
.TP
.BR \-\-corpus " " DIR
Use a real corpus directory instead of the synthetic one.
.TP
.BR \-\-queries " " N
Time at most
.I N
queries (0 means all of them).
.TP
.BR \-\-repeats " " N
Timing repetitions per query (default: 3).
.TP
.BR \-\-limit " " N
Results per query (default: 10).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-embed
Full\-text benchmark only.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-db
Keep the throwaway database for inspection.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the result as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-\-out " " FILE
Write the result to
.I FILE
as JSON.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the help for a command and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/feagle/config.toml
Configuration: roots, limits, model, search knobs, launcher and openers. Every
key is documented in the file itself.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/feagle/gui.toml
Settings of the launcher popup ("[popup]" table: preview, theme, row layout and
filter). Written by the popup through the daemon; a wrong value is reported and
ignored instead of being applied.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/feagle/feagle.sqlite
The index: one SQLite database (file mode 0600, directory 0700) with the file
table, the full\-text index and the vectors.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/feagle/models/
Downloaded GGUF models and the multimodal projector.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/feagle/
Frecency history, llama\-server logs and other user state.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/feagle/queryd.sock
Unix socket of the query daemon (0600). The same runtime directory holds the
coordination files of the shared
.B llama-server
(port, pid, lock and activity stamp).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FEAGLE_LOG_LEVEL
Log level for this process:
.BR DEBUG ", " INFO ", " WARNING
or
.BR ERROR .
Interactive commands default to
.BR WARNING ,
the daemons to
.BR INFO .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME ", " XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Respected for every file above; nothing is hard\-coded to a home directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A runtime failure: the index is missing, the daemon is not running, a file
cannot be opened, and so on. The message goes to standard error.
.TP
.B 2
A configuration or usage error: an unreadable or invalid configuration file, or
bad arguments.
.SH NOTES
.SS Degradation
Without
.B llama-server
or a model, search uses the full\-text index only, and
.B feagle doctor
lists what is missing. Optional extractors degrade the same way: no poppler
means PDF files are skipped, no tesseract means OCR is skipped, no whisper.cpp
means audio is left unsupported.
.SS Privacy
The index and the socket belong to the user (0600/0700). The
.B preview
operation of the query daemon serves only files that are in the index, so access
to the socket does not become access to arbitrary files.
.B llama-server
listens on 127.0.0.1 only.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.exec (5),
.BR pdftotext (1),
.BR tesseract (1)
.PP
The full documentation, with launcher and compositor examples, is in the project
README (the AUR package installs it as
.IR /usr/share/doc/feagle/README.md )
and in the configuration file itself.
